{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: Failure message is maintained in three copies**

In this branch the same information is emitted three times:

1. `console.error(PR_LOOKUP_FAILED_PREFIX + ' no Pull Request found ...')` (this line)
2. `throw new Error(PR_LOOKUP_FAILED_PREFIX + ' no Pull Request found ...')` — a near-identical 4-line message
3. the outer catch logs it again (`console.error('❌ Error in pushReworkChanges:', error)`) and posts it to the tracker

Two nearly-identical string blobs in one branch will drift apart on the next edit (they already differ subtly). The leg log, job summary and tracker comment all get the thrown message anyway, so the pre-throw `console.error` adds little:

```js
if (!pr) {
    // Loud failure instead of silent skip (fa #1212, 2026-10-04): the silent skip
    // left threads unresolved, closed the cycle, and re-armed empty laps forever.
    throw new Error(PR_LOOKUP_FAILED_PREFIX +
        ' no Pull Request found for ticket ' + ticketKey +
        " after the rework push (branch '" + branchName + "'). Review-thread replies/resolutions and the" +
        ' fix-summary comment were NOT posted; the rework cycle was NOT closed — failing loudly instead of' +
        ' silently skipping (silent skip re-arms empty rework laps forever).');
}
```

Purely a maintainability nit — behavior is correct as written.
