{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: The `pr-N` anchor convention is now copy-pasted in 5 places — extract a shared helper**

This PR adds two more copies of the anchor regex:

- `js/common/githubHelpers.js:138` (this change)
- `js/pushReworkChanges.js:157` (this change)
- plus the pre-existing `js/preCliReworkSetup.js:105`, `js/preparePRForReview.js:23`, `js/postPRReviewComments.js:787`

The convention ("lowercase `pr-<digits>` IS the PR number, case-sensitive so real Jira keys like `PR-1212` keep the scan") lives only in comments. If it ever changes — e.g. supporting an `mr-N` GitLab twin, trimming whitespace, or admitting uppercase — five scattered regexes must be found and updated in lockstep, and a miss produces exactly the kind of half-anchored inconsistency this PR fixes.

Suggested: export the predicate/extractor once next to the lookup that consumes it:

```js
// js/common/githubHelpers.js
function extractPrAnchorNumber(ticketKey) {
    var m = /^pr-(\d+)$/.exec(String(ticketKey || ''));
    return m ? m[1] : null;   // null → not a PR-anchored key
}
```

...and use it in all five sites. `pushReworkChanges.findPRForTicket` could then simply delegate every key to `ghHelpers.findPRForTicket` anchored-check first, dropping its own copy. Follow-up refactor — nothing here blocks the merge.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment3.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: New `!repoInfo` throw branch has no test coverage**

The `!pr` loud-failure path is thoroughly covered (`loud failure: PR lookup fails → leg fails...` asserts `success:false`, the greppable marker, no PR comment, no In-Review move, no label removal). The sibling branch introduced in the same hunk — `repoInfo` null (no `config.repository`, unparsable git remote) — throws the same `PR-LOOKUP-FAILED` error but is untested.

A one-fixture test would mirror the existing one and lock the contract in:

```js
test('loud failure: unparsable repository info also fails loudly instead of silently skipping', function() {
    var fx = loadAnchoredAction({
        getRemoteRepoInfo: function() { return null; }
    });
    // also pass config without repository: loadPushReworkChangesForAction's
    // baseConfig would need a repository-free variant
    var result = fx.run();

    assert.equal(result.success, false);
    assert.contains(String(result.error), 'PR-LOOKUP-FAILED');
    assert.contains(String(result.error), 'could not determine the GitHub repository');
    assert.equal(fx.moveCalls.filter(function(s) { return s === 'In Review'; }).length, 0,
        'cycle not closed');
    assert.equal(fx.removedLabels.length, 0, 'no label removal');
});
```

Note the branch runs *after* `commitAndPush`, so the fixture's push mocks already satisfy it — only the repo-info source needs stubbing (plus a `config.repository`-free base config so the `config.repository` short-circuit doesn't mask the stub).
